torch.cuda.synchronize()
elapsed = torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True) ...

# Pattern B: distributed components hardcode CUDA availability
if torch.cuda.is_available():
    ...  # decides whether to create the gloo mesh dim group
handle = torch.cuda.current_device()
```

**Proposed decoupling approach.** Replace the CUDA-specific symbols with their generic equivalents:

### Proposal 3-A: `torch.cuda.*` → `torch.accelerator.*`

| CUDA-specific usage | Generic equivalent |
|---------------------|--------------------|
| `torch.cuda.is_available()` | `torch.accelerator.is_available()` |
| `torch.cuda.current_device()` | `torch.accelerator.current_device_index()` |
| `torch.cuda.synchronize()` | `torch.accelerator.synchronize()` |
| `torch.cuda.current_stream()` | `torch.accelerator.current_stream()` |
| `torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True)` | `torch.Event(enable_timing=True)` |
| `device="cuda"` default value | `torch.accelerator.current_accelerator(check_available=True)`, falling back to `"cpu"` |
| When per-device dispatch is needed | `torch.get_device_module(device)` / `get_interface_for_device(device)` |

