body_text:
### Describe the bug

With `quarkus-undertow`, a `Range` request for a static resource in `META-INF/resources` returns a 206 with the right headers, but wrong content: part of the body is replaced by zero bytes and everything after it is shifted, so the end of the range is lost. A plain GET (200) returns the right content.

### Expected behavior

The body of the 206 response is exactly the requested range of the file.

### Actual behavior

The body has the expected length, but it contains a block of zeros and the content after it is shifted.

To check it, I download the whole file, then request it again from byte 100000 to the end, and compare the second response with the same range taken from the full download:

```
$ curl -s -o full.txt -w '%{http_code} %{size_download}\n' http://localhost:8080/big.txt
200 1048580

$ curl -s -o part.txt -H "Range: bytes=100000-" -D - -w '%{http_code} %{size_download}\n' http://localhost:8080/big.txt
HTTP/1.1 206 Partial Content
Content-Type: text/plain
Last-Modified: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 07:36:38 GMT
Accept-Ranges: bytes
Content-Range: bytes 100000-1048579/1048580
Content-Length: 948580

206 948580

$ tail -c +100001 full.txt | cmp - part.txt
- part.txt differ: byte 14549, line 225

$ head -c 14560 part.txt | tail -c 32 | xxd
00000000: 740a 3030 3030 3137 3632 206c 6f72 656d  t.00001762 lorem
00000010: 2069 7073 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000   ips............
```
Status, headers and length of the 206 are correct, but the content differs from byte 14549 on: the text stops in the middle of a line and is followed by zeros.

### How to Reproduce?

[undertow-range-repro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33093741/undertow-range-repro.zip)


The reproducer attached contains:

1.  A project with only `quarkus-undertow`.
2.  A text file of about 1 MB in `src/main/resources/META-INF/resources/big.txt`.

In order to execute it:

1. `mvn package` and `java -jar target/quarkus-app/quarkus-run.jar`. I only tried with the packaged app, where the resource is a `jar:` URL.
2. Run the curl commands above. Or the following test, which fails with `array contents differ at index [14548], expected: <117> but was: <0>`:


```java
@QuarkusIntegrationTest
class RangeRequestIT {

    @Test
    void rangeRequestReturnsExactlyTheRequestedBytes() {
        byte[] full = given().get("/big.txt").then().statusCode(200).extract().asByteArray();

        int start = 100_000;
        byte[] part = given().header("Range", "bytes=" + start + "-")
                .get("/big.txt").then().statusCode(206).extract().asByteArray();

        assertEquals(full.length - start, part.length);
        assertArrayEquals(Arrays.copyOfRange(full, start, full.length), part);
    }
}
```

Reproducer attached, 

### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`

Microsoft Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200.

### Output of `java -version`

java version "21.0.7" 2025-04-15 LTS

### Quarkus version or git rev

3.40.1 (quarkus-http 5.5.0). 

### Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`)

Apache Maven 3.9.5

### Additional information

The `DefaultServlet` serves range requests with `URLResource#serveRangeBlocking`:

https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus-http/blob/5.5.0/core/src/main/java/io/undertow/server/handlers/resource/URLResource.java#L360-L366

In the chunk where the range starts, `sw` bytes are skipped but `ew` is still `r`, so `write(buffer, offset + sw, r)` goes `sw` bytes past the data that was read. With this change the test above passes on both 3.40.1 and 3.33.2.1 (I tried it by putting a patched copy of the class in the app):

```diff
-        int pos = 0;
+        long pos = 0;
 ...
                 if (rem <= 0) {
                     sender.close();
                     return;
-                } else if (r > rem) {
-                    ew = rem;
                 } else {
-                    ew = r;
+                    ew = Math.min(r - sw, rem);
                 }
```

`pos` is an `int`, so it would also overflow for resources larger than 2 GB. The code is the same in quarkus-http `main`.

