## Describe the bug

`AutoAddScopeBuildItem.Builder.implementsInterface()` enters an infinite loop when a class's superclass is not present in the Jandex index. This is a regression of #12102, which was fixed in 1.8.1 via PR #12103.

The original fix added `else { superName = null; }` to break out of the while loop in `AutoAddScopeProcessor`. When the `implementsInterface` logic was later moved to `AutoAddScopeBuildItem.Builder` (around the time of #11700), the fix was not carried over.

## Current code (3.32.2 and main)

```java
// AutoAddScopeBuildItem.java line ~222
public Builder implementsInterface(DotName interfaceName) {
    return and((clazz, annotations, index) -> {
        if (clazz.interfaceNames().contains(interfaceName)) {
            return true;
        }
        DotName superName = clazz.superName();
        while (superName != null && !superName.equals(DotNames.OBJECT)) {
            ClassInfo superClass = index.getClassByName(superName);
            if (superClass != null) {
                if (superClass.interfaceNames().contains(interfaceName)) {
                    return true;
                }
                superName = superClass.superName();
            }
            // BUG: no else branch — superName is never updated when superClass is null
        }
        return false;
    });
}
```

When `index.getClassByName(superName)` returns `null` (superclass not in any Jandex index), `superName` is never updated. The while condition remains true, and the loop spins forever at 100% CPU.

## Expected fix

Same as the original #12103:

```java
if (superClass != null) {
    if (superClass.interfaceNames().contains(interfaceName)) {
        return true;
    }
    superName = superClass.superName();
} else {
    superName = null; // or break;
}
```

## How to reproduce

1. Have a dependency JAR with a Jandex index containing a class that extends a class from another module
2. Do NOT include that other module on the classpath
3. Run any `@QuarkusTest` — the build hangs in `AutoAddScopeProcessor$1.transform()` → `AutoAddScopeBuildItem.test()` → `implementsInterface` lambda

Thread dump shows:
```
at org.jboss.jandex.CompositeIndex.getClassByName(CompositeIndex.java:270)
at io.quarkus.arc.processor.IndexClassLookupUtils.getClassByName(IndexClassLookupUtils.java:47)
at io.quarkus.arc.processor.BeanArchives$IndexWrapper.getClassByName(BeanArchives.java:131)
at io.quarkus.arc.deployment.AutoAddScopeBuildItem$Builder.lambda$implementsInterface$3(AutoAddScopeBuildItem.java:222)
...
at io.quarkus.arc.processor.BeanDeployment.isVetoed(BeanDeployment.java:1446)
at io.quarkus.arc.processor.BeanDeployment.findBeans(BeanDeployment.java:1153)
```

## Workaround

Either:
- Exclude the problematic class via `quarkus.arc.exclude-types`
- Add the missing module as an optional/test dependency

## Environment

- Quarkus 3.32.2 (also confirmed present on `main` branch / 3.36.3)
- JDK 21 and JDK 26
- macOS / Linux

